; The format is in Tutorials.md: four beats per key -- say the key with the
; word it comes from, press it, hear the reader word for word, say what that
; meant. Name silence. Name no screen reader. Ten walks in the pattern of ten,
; each three to five minutes, in the Homer pattern the kit itself prescribes. Where the kit has
; no screen of its own, an app built on it -- DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir -- shows
; what the kit's code makes a person hear.

FileTask = tutorial

[feed]
Title=HomerDev Walkthroughs
Description=Spoken walks through the Homer Development Kit: what it is, how it builds and releases an app, and what its shared code makes a person hear. Ten walks in the pattern of ten, each three to five minutes.
Author=Jamal Mazrui
Email=jamal.mazrui@outlook.com
Base=

[about]
Title=0 - Overview
Intro=What the Homer Development Kit is, in a paragraph; the two reader keys every walk assumes; then the table of contents, one line per walk.
Setup=Nothing is needed; this walk is listened to.
Homework=Listen to the walks in order; each one assumes the ones before it.

[step]

Say=HomerDev is a kit of parts for building Windows programs that work well by keyboard and screen reader: shared C sharp classes and Python modules, build and release scripts, installer parts, templates for a new app, and skills that teach an AI assistant the house rules. Every decision that makes a program pleasant to use without sight -- where the focus goes, what is spoken, what the keys do -- has been made once and put in a class, so an app built on the kit inherits it. DbDo, EdSharp and FileDir are built on it, and these walks use their voices to show what the kit's code does for a person.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=You know your screen reader's own keys already, and three of them are worth remembering whenever you feel lost or unsure. Insert plus Up Arrow says the line you are on again.
Key=Insert+Up Arrow
Hear=Hello, world.

[step]

Say=Insert plus Tab says what has the focus: its name, its role, and its value or state.
Key=Insert+Tab
Hear=Untitled, edit, multiline, Hello, world.

[step]

Say=Insert plus T says the title of the window.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=EdSharp, Untitled

[step]

Say=If you set your screen reader to use Caps Lock in place of Insert, Caps Lock works the same way for all three.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Now the table of contents. I say the number and the title; the reader says what the walk covers.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=One, User Interface.
Key=
Hear=What a Homer program is made of, heard in DbDo, EdSharp and FileDir, and the rules every key follows, so a key can be guessed.

[step]

Say=Two, Install and Launch.
Key=
Hear=Unarchiving the kit, running its own build, and launching the sample program it builds.

[step]

Say=Three, Start an App from the Kit.
Key=
Hear=A new app from the template: its files, its first build, its first run.

[step]

Say=Four, Build, Check and Release.
Key=
Hear=What build does, stage by stage; what check refuses; what release publishes.

[step]

Say=Five, The Installer and Its Finish Page.
Key=
Hear=The shared installer parts: boxes that say their state, the results box, the summary.

[step]

Say=Six, Spoken Tutorials.
Key=
Hear=Writing a walk, the two voices, the pattern of ten, and the tool that speaks and measures them.

[step]

Say=Seven, Shared Code and the Homer Player.
Key=
Hear=The classes every app uses, and the player heard in FileDir and DbDo alike.

[step]

Say=Eight, Build with an AI Assistant.
Key=
Hear=A feature written with an AI assistant in the kit's house style: the skills, the three sentences, and the check that proves it.

[step]

Say=Nine, Conclusion.
Key=
Hear=The conclusion and summary, the words the kit uses, the help built into every program, and where to learn more.

[step]

Say=Ten walks, three to five minutes each, under an hour together: the overview, the user interface, seven tasks, and the conclusion. They are a course, not a reference: each one assumes those before it.
Key=
Hear=
